465 0 obj
<<
/A 2252 0 R
/Alt (The four panel diagram shows the MRAMnet architecture for diabetic retinopathy grading. Panel a, labelled MRAMnet, shows an input retinal fundus image, augmentation, and two processed retinal images fed into the network. Panel b, labelled Feature Extraction, displays a dual branch design with light blue and light orange rectangular blocks representing feature extraction. The upper branch is labelled Contrastive Branch, leading to a projector and Projection head with DSCLoss. The lower branch is labelled Classification Branch, leading to a projector and ArcFace head with ArcFaceLoss and FocalLoss. Both branches are combined via MixLoss for final DR severity classification. Panel c, labelled multi-region attention module MRAM, illustrates dual branch processing with channel attention, spatial attention, and a transformer with cross attention fusion mechanisms, producing concatenated feature maps as output. Panel d, labelled Contrastive Disentangled Learning, shows a decoupled supervised contrastive loss approach leading to five classification categories: Normal, Mild NPDR, Moderate NPDR, Severe NPDR, and PDR. A legend indicates MRAM Bottleneck, weight sharing, skip connection, and cross attention.)
/K 8
/P 43 0 R
/Pg 15 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
