523 0 obj
<<
/A 2299 0 R
/Alt (The diagram shows the architecture of the Multi-Region Attention Module \(MRAM\). The input feature map at the top-left is partitioned into four quadrant regions, which are processed in parallel through two complementary branches. The first branch contains a Channel Attention Block followed by a Spatial Attention Block with residual connections. The Channel Attention Block processes the feature input through maxpool and avgpool layers, followed by a shared MLP and sigmoid activation, outputting a channel attention map. The Spatial Attention Block processes the channel-refined features through channel-wise maxpool and avgpool, a 7x7 convolution, and sigmoid activation, outputting a spatial attention map. The second branch is a Transformer module that captures long-range dependencies within each region through multi-head self-attention. The two branches are then combined via a cross-attention fusion mechanism that enables bidirectional information exchange between the CNN-based and transformer-based representations. The fused regional features are passed to a Region Interaction Module \(RIM\), which hierarchically aggregates the four quadrant features F1, F2, F3, and F4 through 1x1 convolutions, batch normalization, and ReLU activation &#x02014; first combining horizontally adjacent quadrants, then vertically combining the resulting halves &#x02014; to produce the final output feature map at the bottom-left.)
/K 25
/P 43 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
