/A 2338 0 R
/Alt (The diagram shows two bottleneck structures side by side for comparison. On the left, labelled ResNet Bottleneck, the input is labelled 2048-d in. An upward arrow leads to a green trapezoid labelled 2048, 1&#x000D7;1, 512 \(dimension reduction\). An upward arrow leads to a pink rectangle labelled 512, 3&#x000D7;3, 512 \(standard spatial convolution for feature extraction\). An upward arrow leads to a green trapezoid labelled 512, 1&#x000D7;1, 2048 \(dimension restoration\). An upward arrow leads to a circular node with a plus sign, which then leads to an output labelled 2048-d out. A curved skip connection from the 2048-d input bypasses the three layers and points to the circular node, representing the residual learning framework. On the right, labelled MRAM Bottleneck, the structure is identical except that the middle pink rectangle is replaced by a blue rectangle labelled 512, MRAM, 512, where the standard 3&#x000D7;3 spatial convolution is substituted with the proposed Multi-Region Attention Module \(MRAM\) to capture cross-region dependencies while preserving the residual learning framework.)
