660 0 obj
<<
/A 2416 0 R
/Alt (The two-panel diagram shows data preprocessing and augmentation of fundus images from two datasets. Panel a, labelled Data preprocessing, displays four sequential steps in columns: Original Image, Binary Mask, Contour, and Cropped Image. Each column contains two circular fundus images representing examples from different datasets. The Original Image column shows raw fundus images. The Binary Mask column shows corresponding binary masks generated using the OTSU thresholding method. The Contour column shows the original images overlaid with a red contour line indicating the largest detected contour. The Cropped Image column shows the final images after cropping to remove background, demonstrating adaptability to different image sizes. Panel b, labelled Data enhancement, illustrates the threefold augmentation strategy. The left column displays reference fundus images labelled label 0 and label 1. The right column shows three sets of three augmented images, each marked with a &#x000D7;3 symbol: label 2 &#x000D7;3, label 3 &#x000D7;3, and label 4 &#x000D7;3. The augmented images show variations through random horizontal/vertical flips and scaling, applied specifically to DR stages 2, 3, and 4 to mitigate class imbalance.)
/K 10
/P 43 0 R
/Pg 23 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
