830 0 obj
<<
/A 2475 0 R
/Alt (The figure shows two confusion matrices side by side, comparing the effect of region partitioning on DR classification performance. Each matrix is a 5&#x000D7;5 grid with horizontal and vertical axes labelled 0 to 4, corresponding to the five DR severity grades: No DR, Mild NPDR, Moderate NPDR, Severe NPDR, and PDR. A vertical intensity bar on the right of each panel ranges from 0.0 to 0.8, with darker shades indicating higher values. The left matrix represents the non-partitioned MRAM configuration, with diagonal values of 0.870, 0.917, 0.708, 0.800, and 0.750, showing scattered misclassifications across all severity grades, particularly for moderate and severe stages. The right matrix represents the region-partitioned MRAM configuration, with notably higher diagonal values of 0.941, 0.917, 0.896, 0.900, and 0.929. The right matrix demonstrates significantly improved diagonal dominance and reduced off-diagonal misclassifications, particularly for early-stage lesions \(Grade 1-2\), confirming that the four-quadrant region partitioning strategy enhances classification performance across all DR severity grades.)
/K 41
/P 43 0 R
/Pg 26 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
