869 0 obj
<<
/A 2490 0 R
/Alt (The line graph shows class-wise F1 scores for five different MRAM configurations across the five DR severity stages. The horizontal axis represents DR Stages: No DR, Mild NPDR, Moderate NPDR, Severe NPDR, and PDR. The vertical axis represents F1 Score, ranging from 0.80 to 0.92. Five lines represent the ablation configurations: Without Region Partitioning, Without Transformer Branch, Without Channel-Spatial Attention, Without Cross-Attention Fusion, and Complete MRAM. The Complete MRAM line consistently achieves the highest F1 scores across all stages, starting at approximately 0.89 for No DR, peaking at 0.92 for Mild NPDR, and maintaining strong performance for the clinically critical severe grades \(Severe NPDR and PDR\) where other configurations show notable degradation. The Without Region Partitioning line is consistently the lowest, starting at 0.855 and steadily decreasing to 0.805 for PDR, confirming that region partitioning is the most critical component. The other three configurations show intermediate performance with varying trends across DR stages. The graph highlights that the full MRAMnet architecture provides particularly significant gains for the underrepresented severe DR grades \(Severe NPDR and PDR\), validating the synergistic effect of integrating all four MRAM components.)
/K 39
/P 43 0 R
/Pg 27 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
