1094 0 obj
<<
/A 2573 0 R
/Alt (The four-panel line graph shows accuracy on the vertical axis \(ranging from 85 to 90 percent\) versus four key hyperparameters, with results for APTOS2019 \(solid blue line with square markers\) and EYEPACS \(dashed orange line with triangle markers\). Error bars indicate standard deviation from 5-fold cross-validation, and shaded regions in each panel indicate the recommended operating range. Panel a shows accuracy versus loss weighting factor &#x003BB;_con. The APTOS2019 line increases from 87.5 at 0.1 to a peak of 89.0 at 0.5, then decreases to 87.7 at 0.9. The EYEPACS line increases from 88.5 at 0.1 to a peak of 90.2 at 0.5, then decreases to 88.7 at 0.9, with recommended range [0.3, 0.7]. Panel b shows accuracy versus DSCL temperature &#x003C4;. Both curves peak at &#x003C4; &#x0003D; 0.07, with APTOS2019 reaching 89.1 and EYEPACS reaching 90.1; lower values cause training instability and higher values reduce discrimination of hard negatives. Panel c shows accuracy versus ArcFace margin m, with both curves peaking at m &#x0003D; 0.5 \(89.1 for APTOS2019, 90.2 for EYEPACS\), providing the best balance between inter-class separation and intra-class compactness. Panel d shows accuracy versus DSCL decoupling parameter &#x003B1;, with peaks at &#x003B1; &#x0003D; 0.75 \(89.2 for APTOS2019, 90.2 for EYEPACS\), and stable performance across [0.65, 0.85]. All four panels demonstrate consistent optimal values across both datasets, confirming the robustness of MRAMnet to hyperparameter choices.)
/K 4
/P 43 0 R
/Pg 30 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
